<refentry version="5.1"
  xml:id="Api.SilikoNodeFromError"
  xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook">
<refmeta>
  <refentrytitle>SilikoNodeCreateFromError</refentrytitle>
</refmeta>

<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoNodeCreateFromError</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Function to create an error node</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Node.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">SilikoNode *SilikoNodeCreateFromError(enum SilikoError source);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoNodeCreateFromError</function> function
creates a new <type>SilikoNode</type> object representing an error as
specifyed by <varname>source</varname>.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para><function>SilikoNodeCreateFromError</function> returns a pointer
to a new error <type>SilikoNode</type> object on success, or
<literal>NULL</literal> if there was a memory error.</para>
</refsection>
</refentry>
